            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Penny"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I have made raisin sauce for years but printed this recipe for quantity's as I don't want to look for mine. Unfortunately I believe there is an error in the recipe as one teaspoon of corn starch is NOT enough. I expect it was suppose to be one tablespoon. Tasted good but it did not thicken.",
            "datePublished": "2024-04-01T01:04:26.206Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "SandyPear3898"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I needed more corn starch than suggested. Tapping tiny amounts out of a teaspoon it lumped up very easily; I ended up using a flour sifter to add specks at a time. Also added powdered cloves (maybe half a teaspoon?) and a tablespoon of butter to enrich the flavor.",
            "datePublished": "2023-11-22T23:45:18.766Z"
          },
          {
